# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in your keys. backend/.env is gitignored.

# Required — https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional — any OpenRouter model id that supports structured outputs.
# Checked against OpenRouter's live model list at startup.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4.1-mini

# Required — https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com (Search plan)
BRAVE_API_KEY=

# Optional — which code writes the morning briefing: genkit (the default,
# through Genkit for Go) or legacy (the original OpenRouter client). Switch
# back to legacy if the Genkit briefing misbehaves.
# KINLIGHT_BRIEFER=genkit

# Optional — the Genkit model the briefing uses. Defaults to
# openrouter/ + OPENROUTER_MODEL, so both briefers use the same model.
# GENKIT_MODEL=openrouter/openai/gpt-4.1-mini

# Kid chat — a separate OpenRouter key just for the kids' conversations.
# Every kid call through it is restricted to zero-data-retention providers
# that don't collect data. Without it, kid chat is off ("Chat isn't set up
# yet. Ask a parent."). Create it at https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys.
# OPENROUTER_KIDS_API_KEY=
# The models kid chat uses. Each needs a zero-data-retention endpoint
# (`make ai-smoke` checks) whose provider doesn't block what a kid in
# trouble writes (`make ai-eval-kids` checks). The OpenAI models' ZDR
# endpoints block self-harm messages, so don't use them here.
# KIDS_CHAT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5
# KIDS_SAFETY_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5

# The parents' Assistant model. "Ask anything" uses it on the main key;
# "About the kids" uses it on the kids' key, so it also needs a
# zero-retention endpoint that doesn't block (`make ai-smoke` checks).
# PARENT_CHAT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5

# Optional — MiniMax's Anthropic-compatible API, for the owner's own use and
# experiments only. Never route kids' conversations to it: it isn't a
# no-retention provider. Leave the key unset to keep MiniMax out entirely.
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=
# MINIMAX_BASE_URL=https://api.minimax.io/anthropic
# MINIMAX_MODEL=MiniMax-M3.1-Flash

# Optional — the Go API listens on 127.0.0.1:$PORT
PORT=8080

# Optional — the SQLite database file (created on first run)
DB_PATH=kinlight.db

# Optional — only for pointing the backend at fake servers in tests.
# Leave these unset to use the real APIs.
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# BRAVE_BASE_URL=https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1

# Local development only — never set these in a deployment.
# Answer the demo family's calendar links (https://fixtures.kinlight.test/...)
# with generated feeds. `make demo-serve` turns this on for you.
# KINLIGHT_DEV_FIXTURES=1
# Let kid chat use any provider (with the main key if there's no kids' key),
# for prototyping with the demo family. Never set it once the kids use the app.
# KINLIGHT_KIDS_ALLOW_RETENTION=1
# Start Genkit's reflection server for the Dev UI (`make dev-ui` sets
# GENKIT_ENV=dev for you). It runs AI flows without a login.
# GENKIT_ENV=dev
# Use a real private calendar link for a demo member instead of their fixture.
# `make demo` writes these only into kinlight.db.demo and never prints them.
# SEED_CALENDAR_MAYA=
# SEED_CALENDAR_SAM=
# SEED_CALENDAR_JORDAN=
# SEED_CALENDAR_ALEX=

# Public landing links (optional, HTTPS URLs without credentials).
KINLIGHT_DEMO_URL=
KINLIGHT_VIDEO_URL=
# Hosted judge demo is a separate deployment: see docs/judge-demo.md.
